 * model at all yet) -- see src/process.rs's do_setpgid in the OxideBSD tree. A real, if narrow,
 * numeric collision this remap itself introduces: getresgid's own untouched-from-Linux value is
 * also 120 -- no caller in this port reaches getresgid, so this hasn't bitten anything, but it
 * would silently land on setpgid's own handler instead of cleanly failing if one ever did (the
 * same kind of "flagged, not fixed, since nothing reaches it yet" collision open's own remap once
