/* OxideBSD's own invention (150, continuing right past SYS_socketpair = 149). Called unconditionally
 * by every musl-linked program at startup (src/env/__init_tls.c) and again after every real fork()
 * (src/process/_Fork.c), storing the result as the calling thread's own tid -- previously entirely
 * unregistered, so every process here silently ran with tid = -ENOSYS the whole time (harmless so
 * far, nothing reads pthread_self()->tid for anything correctness-critical, but a real gap found
 * while tracing an unrelated wget HTTPS failure). No real threading exists on this kernel, so tid
 * and pid are the same concept -- src/syscall.rs's sys_set_tid_address just echoes the caller's
 * own pid back, ignoring the tidptr argument entirely (no clear_child_tid futex-wake to honor
 * without real pthread_create-spawned threads). */
